---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /
# The search-facing metadata is category-level: OpenEduOps covers open-source
# learning platforms, of which Moodle and Open edX are the two covered so far.
# No ogTitle override here, so Open Graph and Twitter carry the same title.
title: OpenEduOps | Open-Source Learning Infrastructure Tutorials
description: Practical tutorials for installing, securing, and operating open-source learning platforms, including Moodle and Open edX, with verification and guides.
structuredData:
  - "@context": https://schema.org
    "@type": WebSite
    name: OpenEduOps
    url: https://openeduops.com/
  - "@context": https://schema.org
    "@type": Organization
    name: OpenEduOps
    url: https://openeduops.com/
    logo: https://openeduops.com/assets/logo/openeduops-lockup-light.png
    sameAs:
      - https://www.youtube.com/@OpenEduOps
      - https://github.com/OpenEduOpsLabs
      - https://x.com/OpenEduOps
---

<!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
<section class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="shell hero-inner">

    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-on-dark">Self-hosted open learning</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Build it.<br>Secure it.<br>Understand it.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">Open-source learning platforms, from infrastructure to verified operation.</p>
      <p class="hero-text">OpenEduOps publishes practical, production-aware tutorials for building and
        operating open-source learning platforms, connecting Moodle and Open edX with the
        infrastructure, security, automation, and operations behind them.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/tutorials/">Browse tutorials</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#platforms">Choose a learning path</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-visual">
      <!-- The stack the LMS actually runs on: platform → infrastructure → security → operations -->
      <svg class="stack" viewBox="0 0 540 470" role="img" aria-labelledby="stack-title stack-desc">
        <title id="stack-title">The system beneath a learning platform</title>
        <desc id="stack-desc">A learning platform layer — Moodle or Open edX — sitting on a web and
          application layer, a data and storage layer, and a server and network layer. The lower three
          layers sit inside a security boundary, and the whole stack connects to backup, monitoring,
          and automation.</desc>

        <!-- spine + traces -->
        <g class="stack-traces" fill="none" stroke="#4A5A72" stroke-width="2">
          <path d="M40 46 V 402" />
          <path d="M40 46 H 92" />
          <path d="M40 152 H 92" />
          <path d="M40 258 H 92" />
          <path d="M40 344 H 92" />
          <path d="M40 402 H 200 M280 402 H 340 M420 402 H 470" />
        </g>
        <path class="stack-signal" d="M40 46 V 402" fill="none" stroke="#FF6B35" stroke-width="2"
              stroke-linecap="round" stroke-dasharray="26 330" />

        <!-- security boundary around infrastructure layers -->
        <g class="stack-boundary">
          <rect x="20" y="118" width="500" height="260" rx="16" fill="none"
                stroke="#7d8a9c" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3 7" />
          <text class="stack-tag" x="520" y="108" text-anchor="end">SECURITY BOUNDARY</text>
        </g>

        <!-- layers -->
        <g class="layer" data-layer="1">
          <rect x="92" y="10" width="420" height="72" rx="10" />
          <text class="layer-name" x="116" y="44">LEARNING PLATFORM</text>
          <text class="layer-detail" x="116" y="66">Moodle · Open edX · courses · users</text>
        </g>
        <g class="layer" data-layer="2">
          <rect x="92" y="116" width="420" height="72" rx="10" />
          <text class="layer-name" x="116" y="150">WEB + APPLICATION</text>
          <text class="layer-detail" x="116" y="172">Web server · PHP · HTTPS · email</text>
        </g>
        <g class="layer" data-layer="3">
          <rect x="92" y="222" width="420" height="72" rx="10" />
          <text class="layer-name" x="116" y="256">DATA + STORAGE</text>
          <text class="layer-detail" x="116" y="278">Database · files · cache</text>
        </g>
        <g class="layer" data-layer="4">
          <rect x="92" y="308" width="420" height="56" rx="10" />
          <text class="layer-name" x="116" y="342">SERVER + NETWORK</text>
        </g>

        <!-- nodes on the spine -->
        <g class="stack-nodes">
          <circle cx="40" cy="46" r="7" />
          <circle cx="40" cy="152" r="7" />
          <circle cx="40" cy="258" r="7" />
          <circle cx="40" cy="344" r="7" />
        </g>

        <!-- operations rail -->
        <g class="ops">
          <circle cx="212" cy="402" r="6" />
          <circle cx="352" cy="402" r="6" />
          <circle cx="482" cy="402" r="6" />
          <text class="ops-label" x="212" y="434" text-anchor="middle">BACKUP</text>
          <text class="ops-label" x="352" y="434" text-anchor="middle">MONITOR</text>
          <text class="ops-label" x="482" y="434" text-anchor="middle">AUTOMATE</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ CHOOSE YOUR PLATFORM ============ -->
<section class="section section-sunken" id="platforms">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Choose your platform</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Two platforms, one method.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">Both learning paths follow the same approach: make the change, explain why
        it matters, verify the result, and keep the recovery path visible.</p>
    </header>

    <ul class="platform-grid reveal">
      {%- for platform in site.platforms %}
        {%- include "components/series-card.njk" %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ START HERE ============ -->
<section class="section" id="start-here">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Start here</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">The first step on each path.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">If you have not built either platform before, these are the two places to
        begin.</p>
    </header>

    <ul class="starts reveal">
      {%- for entry in catalogue.startHere %}
        <li class="start">
          <p class="badge badge-{{ entry.platform.slug }}">{{ entry.platform.name }}</p>
          <h3>
            <a href="{{ entry.tutorial.destination.url }}"
               data-event="{{ entry.tutorial.destination.event }}"
               {%- if entry.tutorial.destination.external %} rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ entry.tutorial.title }}</a>
          </h3>
          <p>{{ entry.tutorial.outcome }}</p>
          <p class="meta-row">
            <span>{{ entry.tutorial.stepLabel }}</span>
            <span>{{ entry.tutorial.display_duration }}</span>
          </p>
        </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ LATEST TUTORIALS ============ -->
<section class="section section-sunken" id="latest">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head-row reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Latest tutorials</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Most recently published.</h2>
      </div>
      <a class="action" href="/tutorials/">Browse all {{ catalogue.counts.total }} tutorials</a>
    </header>

    <ul class="card-grid reveal">
      {%- for tutorial in catalogue.latest %}
        {%- include "components/tutorial-card.njk" %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ BUILD / SECURE / OPERATE ============ -->
<section class="section" id="pillars">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">What the tutorials cover</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">One platform, three responsibilities.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">Build, secure, and operate are not separate subjects. They are the same
        system seen at three moments in its life.</p>
    </header>

    <ol class="pillar-track">
      {%- for pillar in site.responsibilities %}
      <li class="pillar reveal reveal-delay-{{ loop.index0 }}">
        <p class="pillar-index">{{ pillar.index }}</p>
        <h3 class="pillar-name">{{ pillar.name }}</h3>
        <p class="pillar-claim">{{ pillar.claim }}</p>
        <p class="pillar-text">{{ pillar.text }}</p>
        <ul class="tag-row">
          {%- for tag in pillar.tags %}<li>{{ tag }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
        <a class="action" href="/tutorials/?responsibility={{ pillar.slug }}#catalogue">{{ catalogue.counts.byResponsibility[pillar.name] }} {{ pillar.name }} tutorials<span class="visually-hidden"> in the catalogue</span></a>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ THE METHOD ============ -->
<section class="section section-sunken" id="method">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">The method</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">More than commands.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">OpenEduOps tutorials show the change, explain why it matters, verify the
        result, and make the operational boundaries visible.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="principles">
      <article class="principle reveal">
        <h3>Understand the change</h3>
        <p>Know what a command or configuration actually affects.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle reveal">
        <h3>Verify the result</h3>
        <p>Do not treat successful execution alone as proof.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle reveal">
        <h3>Prepare for failure</h3>
        <p>Backups, rollback, and recovery are part of the procedure.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle reveal">
        <h3>Keep the boundaries clear</h3>
        <p>A working lab, public demonstration system, and production environment are not the same thing.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ FINAL ACTION ============ -->
<section class="section final-cta" id="start">
  <div class="shell final-inner">
    <h2 class="final-title">Start building.</h2>
    <p class="final-text">{{ catalogue.counts.total }} published long-form tutorials across Moodle and
      Open edX, each with a companion command guide.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/tutorials/">Browse all tutorials</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="{{ site.external.youtube }}" rel="noopener">Watch on YouTube</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
